<title>USA: General Mills raises quarterly dividend.</title>
<headline>General Mills raises quarterly dividend.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Mills Inc. said Monday it will raise its quarterly dividend by three cents to 53 cents per share as of May 1.</p>
<p>The new annual rate of $2.12 represents a 6 percent increase over dividends of $2 paid during the past year.</p>
<p>&quot;This dividend increase reflects General Mills' continued growth momentum and strong financial position,&quot; said Chairman Steve Sanger.</p>
<p>Minneapolis-based General Mills' stock edged down 12.5 cents to $67.625 on the New York Stock Exchange.</p>
</text>
